## Anatomy

`content` (padded) · `children[]` (stable index) · `overflowed` · `content_main` · `direction`

## Usage

```rust
use termrock::layout::{
    Stack, Inline, FlexSize, Align, Justify, OverflowPolicy, direction_for_width,
};

let layout = Stack::new().gap(1).layout(area, &[
    FlexSize::Fixed(2),
    FlexSize::fill(),
    FlexSize::Fixed(1),
]);
let body = layout.get(1).unwrap();

let chips = Inline::new().wrap(true).gap(1).layout(area, &[
    FlexSize::Fixed(6),
    FlexSize::Fixed(6),
]);

// Responsive: stack when narrow, inline when wide
let layout = Stack::new()
    .responsive(area.width, 60)
    .gap(1)
    .layout(area, &[FlexSize::fill(), FlexSize::fill()]);

// Clip tail under pressure
let tight = Stack::new()
    .overflow(OverflowPolicy::ClipTail)
    .layout(area, &[FlexSize::Fixed(3), FlexSize::Fixed(3), FlexSize::Fixed(3)]);

// Intrinsic cross-axis size (non-stretch)
let row = Inline::new()
    .align(Align::Center)
    .layout_with_cross(area, &[FlexSize::Fixed(8)], &[1]);
```

## FlexSize

| Spec | Main-axis claim |
|------|-----------------|
| `Fixed(n)` | Exact `n` (clamped under overflow) |
| `Weight(w)` / `fill()` | Share residual after fixed/preferred |
| `Preferred { min, preferred, max }` | Ideal clamp; may grow to max when free residual |
| `Collapsed` | Zero main; keeps stable index |

## Overflow

| Policy | Behavior |
|--------|----------|
| `ShrinkFromEnd` (default) | From the end: `min(claim, remaining)` |
| `ClipTail` | Keep head; tail → 0 |
| `EqualShare` | Peel cells from the end until fit |

`StackLayout::overflowed` is set when any fixed/preferred child falls below `min_main`.

